//! The `bsc fin` verbs.
//!
//! READ-ONLY SO FAR, and deliberately: `parse` proves the ingest against a file and prints what it
//! found without writing anything. A store lands next, and it lands after the parse is trustworthy —
//! a store filled by a parser nobody has checked is a confident wrong answer that persists.
//!
//! THE RENDERING IS SPLIT OUT FROM `run` ON PURPOSE. `run` does file IO and calls `println!`, and
//! neither can be asserted on; a verb whose whole job is REPORTING therefore had no test at all,
//! which is precisely backwards for the one surface a person reads a balance off. `render_text` and
//! `render_json` are pure — a `Parsed` in, a string in hand — so what this prints is a fact a test
//! can hold rather than something that has to be run and eyeballed.
